{
  "law": "NAVIGATOR-VISION-006 §1 (H1–H9 detection table, v1.2.0) + PHASE_04 Gate 4.1 + PHASE_08E Gate 8E.1. One row per matrix case: the classifier MUST return exactly `expect` for (action, context). `tag`: happy (one per H-class minimum), negative (NOT gated — must classify null AND the mutation net must read ORDINARY, i.e. never even engine-consulted), fail-to-confirm (ambiguous/uncertain resolves to the stricter matching class, never null), additive (the H9 net is SUSPICIOUS: classify is null but RiskGate.mutationNet = SUSPICIOUS — the loop's ADDITIVE-ONLY engine check owns it; a non-LOW answer adds H9, vision 06 §3). H9 detection is a broad net: the verb dictionary here is the illustrative FLOOR (test data, not product law) — novel verbs gate via structure (confirm/flip wording) or via the additive engine check, never by dictionary growth alone. Field descriptors are given as RAW observed attributes (id/label/value/className, plus the reader-captured isPassword flag since the 2026-10-08 pre-UAT2 H8-gap fix) — the test derives isPassword/isCardLike through FieldDescriptor.fromObserved so the derivation itself is under test. This file is a reviewable table: UAT 4.1 has the owner read it and name missing site/form patterns (new rows are additive).",
